1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:04,828
A placed candidate's confirmation mail lands at ten in

2
00:00:04,828 --> 00:00:08,456
the morning. The staffing vendor needs the bill today,

3
00:00:08,456 --> 00:00:09,934
with G S T or without,

4
00:00:09,934 --> 00:00:12,285
and the amount had better be right.

5
00:00:12,285 --> 00:00:15,510
Someone opens a spreadsheet, retypes the figure,

6
00:00:15,510 --> 00:00:17,458
picks a tax rate from memory,

7
00:00:17,458 --> 00:00:18,130
and hopes.

8
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:20,673
What if Claude read the mail,

9
00:00:20,673 --> 00:00:24,322
extracted the amount, checked it against the vendor master,

10
00:00:24,322 --> 00:00:27,476
drafted both versions, and then waited for a person

11
00:00:27,476 --> 00:00:30,197
to say yes before the right one was numbered

12
00:00:30,197 --> 00:00:32,795
or sent? That is bill creation automation,

13
00:00:32,795 --> 00:00:34,650
done with agents, done safely.

14
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:40,045
Gennoor Tech presents Bill Creation Automation with Claude.

15
00:00:40,795 --> 00:00:43,039
One mail in. The right bill out.

16
00:00:43,039 --> 00:00:45,986
You build the pipeline in nine increments,

17
00:00:45,986 --> 00:00:49,142
and every increment is something you can run,

18
00:00:49,142 --> 00:00:51,598
test and demonstrate. Claude reads,

19
00:00:51,598 --> 00:00:55,877
extracts and explains. Deterministic Python computes the tax.

20
00:00:55,877 --> 00:00:58,683
A person approves. Every step is logged,

21
00:00:58,683 --> 00:01:01,840
from the first prompt to the issued document.

22
00:01:02,590 --> 00:01:06,141
You begin with the workflow as it really happens.

23
00:01:06,141 --> 00:01:09,620
Who sends the mail, what a compliant tax invoice

24
00:01:09,620 --> 00:01:12,954
must carry, and when the company issues with G

25
00:01:12,954 --> 00:01:15,274
S T and when it issues a bill of

26
00:01:15,274 --> 00:01:18,825
supply without it. Then you set up the toolchain.

27
00:01:18,825 --> 00:01:21,145
Claude Code on your workstation.

28
00:01:21,145 --> 00:01:23,536
The Claude Agent S D K in Python.

29
00:01:23,536 --> 00:01:26,218
And an M C P server that exposes your

30
00:01:26,218 --> 00:01:30,132
mailbox and vendor master as read-only tools the agent

31
00:01:30,132 --> 00:01:32,017
can call but never bypass.

32
00:01:32,767 --> 00:01:36,522
Then intake. The agent reads each mail through the

33
00:01:36,522 --> 00:01:38,775
Microsoft Graph A P I or I M A

34
00:01:38,775 --> 00:01:41,404
P, including the P D F attachments,

35
00:01:41,404 --> 00:01:44,108
and returns a strict J S O N record:

36
00:01:44,108 --> 00:01:47,638
candidate, vendor, amount, currency, G S T I N,

37
00:01:47,638 --> 00:01:51,769
service period, and a confidence score for every field.

38
00:01:51,769 --> 00:01:56,801
Pydantic validates the record. Anything missing or contradictory is

39
00:01:56,801 --> 00:01:59,505
flagged for a person, never guessed.

40
00:02:00,255 --> 00:02:03,136
On day two the numbers meet the rules.

41
00:02:03,136 --> 00:02:06,168
You load the vendor master into S Q Lite

42
00:02:06,168 --> 00:02:10,338
and reconcile the claimed amount against the rate card,

43
00:02:10,338 --> 00:02:13,750
with a tolerance you control and a reason for

44
00:02:13,750 --> 00:02:16,782
every mismatch. Then you write the G S T

45
00:02:16,782 --> 00:02:19,436
engine as plain Python. C G S T and

46
00:02:19,436 --> 00:02:21,786
S G S T for intra-state supply.

47
00:02:21,786 --> 00:02:23,454
I G S T across states.

48
00:02:23,454 --> 00:02:25,122
H S N and S A C codes,

49
00:02:25,122 --> 00:02:28,610
rounding, and reverse charge where it applies.

50
00:02:28,610 --> 00:02:32,249
Claude explains the computation to the reviewer.

51
00:02:32,249 --> 00:02:33,841
It never performs it.

52
00:02:34,591 --> 00:02:37,373
Then generation. Two versioned templates,

53
00:02:37,373 --> 00:02:39,749
a tax invoice and a bill of supply,

54
00:02:39,749 --> 00:02:42,667
rendered to P D F by the same deterministic

55
00:02:42,667 --> 00:02:45,993
code every time, from the same validated request.

56
00:02:45,993 --> 00:02:49,522
Both previews are drafted; only the one that applies

57
00:02:49,522 --> 00:02:52,915
is ever issued. Invoice numbers live in a sequence

58
00:02:52,915 --> 00:02:55,630
that only the approved path can advance.

59
00:02:55,630 --> 00:02:59,770
Claude drafts the covering mail and the one-paragraph summary

60
00:02:59,770 --> 00:03:02,078
a finance reviewer actually reads.

61
00:03:02,828 --> 00:03:06,598
Day three is guardrails. Every bill enters an approval

62
00:03:06,598 --> 00:03:08,483
queue with the source mail,

63
00:03:08,483 --> 00:03:11,834
the extracted fields, the reconciliation result,

64
00:03:11,834 --> 00:03:15,255
the tax breakdown and both previews side by side.

65
00:03:15,255 --> 00:03:18,606
A person approves in ServiceNow or in the review

66
00:03:18,606 --> 00:03:21,259
C L I. Until then nothing is numbered,

67
00:03:21,259 --> 00:03:24,471
nothing is sent, and the audit log records who

68
00:03:24,471 --> 00:03:26,705
saw what, who decided, and when.

69
00:03:27,455 --> 00:03:29,399
You then harden the pipeline.

70
00:03:29,399 --> 00:03:32,282
Pytest covers the G S T engine across every

71
00:03:32,282 --> 00:03:34,361
rate slab and every state pair,

72
00:03:34,361 --> 00:03:37,512
with golden P D F files guarding the templates.

73
00:03:37,512 --> 00:03:40,931
GitHub Actions runs the suite on every pull request

74
00:03:40,931 --> 00:03:44,551
and push. And approved bills export to your accounting

75
00:03:44,551 --> 00:03:46,429
system as C S V or Tally X M

76
00:03:46,429 --> 00:03:49,848
L, ready for posting, with the mail dispatched only

77
00:03:49,848 --> 00:03:52,664
after the approver's decision is recorded.

78
00:03:53,414 --> 00:03:56,371
Every lab runs on a synthetic mailbox and a

79
00:03:56,371 --> 00:03:59,810
fictional vendor master. You will feed the agent a

80
00:03:59,810 --> 00:04:01,805
mail with a missing G S T I N

81
00:04:01,805 --> 00:04:03,937
and watch it refuse to proceed.

82
00:04:03,937 --> 00:04:07,444
You will trace an over-claim to its rate-card line,

83
00:04:07,444 --> 00:04:10,127
break a rate slab in a pull request and

84
00:04:10,127 --> 00:04:13,084
see the build fail, then approve a bill and

85
00:04:13,084 --> 00:04:15,147
read its complete audit trail.

86
00:04:15,897 --> 00:04:18,505
Here is the full table of contents,

87
00:04:18,505 --> 00:04:20,442
9 modules over three days.

88
00:04:20,442 --> 00:04:24,092
Day one: The vendor bill workflow and the agentic

89
00:04:24,092 --> 00:04:26,551
baseline; Setting up Claude Code,

90
00:04:26,551 --> 00:04:29,084
the Agent SDK and MCP for billing;

91
00:04:29,084 --> 00:04:32,213
and Mail intake and structured extraction.

92
00:04:32,213 --> 00:04:36,907
Day two: Vendor master, amount verification and reconciliation;

93
00:04:36,907 --> 00:04:40,483
The GST computation engine; and Bill generation,

94
00:04:40,483 --> 00:04:43,090
numbering and templates. Day three:

95
00:04:43,090 --> 00:04:46,815
Guardrails, approvals and audit for bill issuance;

96
00:04:46,815 --> 00:04:49,497
Testing, CI and accounting hand-off;

97
00:04:49,497 --> 00:04:53,073
and Capstone: end-to-end bill creation pipeline.

98
00:04:53,823 --> 00:04:58,879
Every build in this course follows six engineering principles.

99
00:04:58,879 --> 00:05:01,081
Model output is a proposal,

100
00:05:01,081 --> 00:05:05,321
never a fact. Authorization lives outside the model.

101
00:05:05,321 --> 00:05:08,909
A human approves every consequential action.

102
00:05:08,909 --> 00:05:11,682
Decisions and evidence are logged.

103
00:05:11,682 --> 00:05:16,493
The stack stays provider-agnostic. And quality is measured,

104
00:05:16,493 --> 00:05:17,471
not assumed.

105
00:05:18,221 --> 00:05:20,438
Nine build steps. Three days,

106
00:05:20,438 --> 00:05:23,955
hands-on. Two drafts from one source of truth,

107
00:05:23,955 --> 00:05:28,236
one bill issued. And zero bills issued without approval.

108
00:05:28,986 --> 00:05:32,258
This course is for enterprise I T and network

109
00:05:32,258 --> 00:05:37,129
operations teams, finance operations and shared-services engineers,

110
00:05:37,129 --> 00:05:41,201
and automation and platform teams in India and worldwide

111
00:05:41,201 --> 00:05:45,418
who want to automate billing without surrendering control.

112
00:05:45,418 --> 00:05:48,398
You need basic Python, comfort with J S O

113
00:05:48,398 --> 00:05:50,943
N, and a working knowledge of G S T

114
00:05:50,943 --> 00:05:51,670
invoicing.

115
00:05:52,420 --> 00:05:55,896
Turn every candidate mail into a correct bill,

116
00:05:55,896 --> 00:05:57,860
with a person in the loop.

117
00:05:57,860 --> 00:06:00,656
Bill Creation Automation with Claude.

118
00:06:00,656 --> 00:06:02,847
Enrol now at gennoor dot com.
